 For LIBERO, we train on a single node with 8 GPUs. For RoboTwin, we use 64 GPUs to accelerate training. You can try reducing the GPU count or training epochs.
 
+## Observation History Conditioning
+
+By default FastWAM conditions on only the current observation `o_t`. Optionally, `K` past
+observations `o_{t-K*s}, ..., o_{t-s}` can be added as extra clean conditioning latents at both
+training and inference time. Enable it in the data config (`configs/data/*.yaml`):
+
+```yaml
+train:
+  num_history_frames: 4 # K past frames; 0 (default) disables history
+  history_stride: 4 # spacing s between history frames, in units of global_sample_stride frames
+```
+
+Details:
+
+- History frames are VAE-encoded frame-by-frame and prepended to the current-frame latent as
+  clean conditioning (timestep 0, excluded from the video loss), generalizing the original
+  first-frame conditioning from 1 to `K+1` latent steps. No new weights are introduced.
+- Near an episode start, missing past frames are placeholder slots that are masked out in
+  attention (`history_is_pad`), so the effective history grows from 0 to `K` real frames as the
+  episode progresses. Placeholder content never conditions the model.
+- The LIBERO / RoboTwin evaluation scripts maintain the observation buffer automatically and
+  pass `history_images` / `history_is_pad` to `infer_action`. History settings are read from
+  `data.train.*` of the task config, so no extra evaluation flags are needed.
+- RoboTwin: with history enabled the policy requests an observation every simulation step,
+  which effectively disables the `EVALUATION.skip_get_obs_within_replan=true` speedup.
+- Evaluate a checkpoint with the same `num_history_frames` / `history_stride` it was trained
+  with.
+
+Unit tests for this feature live in `tests/test_history_conditioning.py` and run on CPU:
+
+```bash
+pytest tests/test_history_conditioning.py
+```
+
 ## Inference with Your Trained Checkpoints
 
 The `mujoco` environment should ideally stay consistent with the LIBERO data version. Then run LIBERO evaluation:
